@nsobid-BBA3811191DE71D9B55E53F918AE5DC1

# ARMS 5.5.1 - 2560x1440 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders at 2560x1440 in both docked and handheld mode.
//
// The engine keeps three sizes: the scan buffer from the Cstm
// getScanBufferSize singleton, which sead::GameFrameworkNx allocates its
// display buffers at and gsys allocates its render buffers at;
// a frame buffer scale that the gfx manager recomputes every frame as
// ladder height / scan buffer height; and a display buffer crop that it
// sets to the absolute ladder size. The ladder holds sizes from 864x486 to
// 1920x1080. Stock play selects entry 7 (1920x1080) docked and entry 3
// (1280x720) handheld at most, some modes and replay scenes cap it lower,
// and unless force_max_resolution is set the scale is also clamped to a
// height cap (1053 lines by default).
//
// The scan buffer and ladder entry 7 are raised to 2560x1440, the selected
// entry is pinned to 7 and the height cap is skipped, so the render, the
// frame buffer and the crop all stay at the full size and the dynamic
// resolution controller can no longer lower them. The 2D canvas is a fixed
// 1280x720 layout space and needs no change.
//
// Two in-match layout managers also size their 3D panel render buffers
// from the selected ladder entry. The panels are drawn into the 1280x720
// layout, and building them at the raised size crashes on match load, so
// both call sites are pinned to the stock maximum of 1920x1080.
//
// Every render target and the cascaded shadow map come from the
// agl::utl::DynamicTextureAllocator pool gsys requests at boot (96 MB). The
// pool is raised to 512 MB, which also leaves room for the
// [Shadow Resolution 4096] mod.
//
// gsys and the pool live in the cGfx heap group partition (1820 MB). Right
// after gsys starts, GfxDynamicHeapMgr takes what is left of cGfx and
// splits 1572 MB of fixed sub-heaps out of it, so stock play leaves gsys at
// most 248 MB. cGfx grows by the pool increase plus 256 MB for the
// render buffers gsys allocates outside the pool, which grow with the
// scan buffer.
//
// sead::GameFrameworkNx creates its display buffers inside the cSys heap
// group partition (491 MB), in a heap that takes everything left and is
// then trimmed, and every Arms and Lp system manager created afterwards
// takes its heap from what remains. Stock boot leaves under 16 MB spare,
// so the larger display buffers leave a later manager with a null heap.
// cSys is raised to 555 MB.
//
// REQUIRES Ryujinx > System > DRAM Size set to 6 GiB or higher. The fixed
// heap group partitions total 3807 MB after this change, more than the
// 3285 MB application pool the default 4 GiB setting provides. The game
// sizes its memory heap from whatever the emulator gives it, so no other
// memory change is needed.
//
// This mod OWNS the pool and heap offsets below; do not duplicate them in
// another enabled mod.

@enabled
// Scan buffer size in both getScanBufferSize getters (was 1920x1080).
00757234 084081D2   // MOVZ X8,#2560
00757238 08B4C0F2   // MOVK X8,#1440,LSL#32
00757460 084081D2   // MOVZ X8,#2560
00757464 08B4C0F2   // MOVK X8,#1440,LSL#32
// Resolution ladder entry 7 (was 1920.0f x 1080.0f).
000CE764 08A4A852   // MOVZ W8,#0x4520,LSL#16 = 2560.0f
000CE768 8996A852   // MOVZ W9,#0x44B4,LSL#16 = 1440.0f
// 3D panel render buffer size in two layout managers (was ladder entry).
0067CEE8 02878052   // MOVZ W2,#1080 (was FCVTZS W2,S1)
0067CEEC 01F08052   // MOVZ W1,#1920 (was FCVTZS W1,S0)
00680FB8 02878052   // MOVZ W2,#1080 (was FCVTZS W2,S1)
00680FBC 01F08052   // MOVZ W1,#1920 (was FCVTZS W1,S0)
// Dynamic resolution controller: always select ladder entry 7.
000CF928 F7008052   // MOVZ W23,#7 (was CSEL W23,W8,W10,EQ)
// Frame buffer scale: skip the height cap.
000D4A64 04000014   // B +0x10 (was TBNZ W8,#3 = force max resolution)
// gsys::SystemTask::CreateArg DynamicTextureAllocator pool.
000D6238 0800A452   // MOVZ W8,#0x2000,LSL#16 = 512 MB (was 96 MB)
// cSys heap group partition, shared by both memory layouts.
0074DE08 0856A452   // MOVZ W8,#0x22B0,LSL#16 = 555 MB (was 491 MB)
// cGfx heap group partition, shared by both memory layouts.
0074DE18 0A78B352   // MOVZ W10,#0x9BC0,LSL#16 = 2492 MB (was 1820 MB)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against ARMS 5.5.1 (Cstm/Lp + gsys/agl +
// sead, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located
// by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
